  "investigation_notes": "Upload failure investigated \u2014 permission failure on uploads directory, not disk or database.\n\n**Status: unhealthy application, uploads failing with 500s**\n\n* Both containers `running`: app `Up 5 seconds`, db `Up 11 seconds (healthy)` (E1).\n* App `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n* App container runs as `1000:1000` with bind `source: /srv/lab-data -> destination: /data, rw: true` (E7).\n\n**Root cause: application user cannot write to uploads directory**\n\n* Host path `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `is_dir: true, owner_uid: 0, owner_gid: 0, mode: 0755, app_uid: 1000, app_gid: 1000, app_user_can_write: false` (E4).\n* Parent `/srv/lab-data` is `owner_uid: 1000, owner_gid: 1000, mode: 0755, app_user_can_write: true` (E9) \u2014 so problem is isolated to `uploads/` subdirectory, not parent mount.\n* App logs prove failure from app's perspective:\n  * `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` followed by `File \"/app/main.py\", line 63, in upload` + `os.replace(tmp_path, final_path)` + `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/...part' -> '/data/uploads/...'` (E5).\n  * Health probe same cause: `health check failed` + `File \"/app/main.py\", line 116, in health` + `with open(probe, \"wb\") as f:` + `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/uploads/.health-...'` + `GET /health 503 Service Unavailable` (E5).\n* Earlier in same log window `POST /upload 200 OK` succeeded (E5), showing uploads stopped working when permissions denied writes.\n\n**Ruled out \u2014 disk full:**\n\n* `/srv/lab-data` filesystem: `use_percent: 9.0, inode_use_percent: 0.2, available_mb: 410.7` (E3).\n* `/` filesystem: `use_percent: 6.8, inode_use_percent: 1.5` (E10).\n\n**Ruled out \u2014 database dependency as cause:**\n\n* Db container `running, health: healthy, oom_killed: false, exit_code: 0` (E11), also `healthy` in list (E1).\n* Db logs: `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors, `Skipping initialization` (E6).\n* App traceback is filesystem `PermissionError`, not DB connection error (E5).\n* Recent events show normal `start` + `health_status: healthy` for db via `pg_isready` (E8).\n\nSymptom vs cause: `500` on `/upload` and `503` on `/health` are symptoms (E5, E2); root cause is host ownership `0:0` on `/srv/lab-data/uploads` blocking uid `1000` writes (E4, E7, E5).\n",
